  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 114 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nWednesday and Thursday, the upper-level high remains in place over \nthe Panhandles, allowing hot and dry conditions to prevail. Thursday \nwe begin to see models trend toward the eastern propagation of \nthe upper-level high pressure, placing the CWA on the western \nextent of the ridge. Perturbations in the upper-level flow could \nlead to daily storm chances across the northwestern combined \nPanhandles. The failure mode of this scenario lies in the \nuncertainty of where this upper-level high will end up. There are \nsignificant long-range model discrepancies in how far east the \nhigh pressure center will propagate, and if it does not push far \nenough east, the best chances of precipitation will likely be \ndisplaced west of the Panhandles. Confidence will increase \nthroughout the week with persistence in model runs and as more \nmodels see the event window, but until then, confidence remains \nlow. \n\nThe high pressure center is currently progged to retrograde back \nwest, placing the Panhandles under the upper-level high again as \nwe go into next week. This will support the return of widespread \ntriple-digit high temperatures and decreased PoP chances if\nconditions stay consistent throughout the week.\n\nFerguson",
